  "program": {
    "module": {
      "summary": "Child Benefit (Rates) Regulations 2006, reg 2 — weekly rate of child\nbenefit.\n\nTwo rates apply:\n  enhanced  £26.05 — eldest child in the household\n  standard  £17.25 — every other child\n\nreg 2(4)(a) disapplies the enhanced rate where the claimant is a\nvoluntary organisation; reg 2(4)(b) disapplies it where the claimant\nresides with a parent of the child (other than as a cohabiting partner).\nThe \"eldest in household\" test (reg 2(2)) cuts across partnered households\n— that legal determination is pre-applied by the caller on each Child\nrecord as `is_eldest_in_household`, as is `resides_with_parent`.\nCombined, `is_enhanced_eligible` on each Child reduces the three-way\ntest to a single boolean the filtered aggregator can count."
    },
